course: dictionary
lesson: 11391
title: Short forms and abbreviations
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Writers often shorten long words to save space. A short form like «acc.» is called an abbreviation. Look for a full stop or a clue from the words around it to work out which full word it stands for.
explain: «Acc» has more than one meaning. On a bank statement, «Acc: 1234» means account. In a grammar book, «the acc. case» means accusative, a grammar case used in languages like German, Latin and Ukrainian. The context tells you which one is right.
explain: In notes and adverts, «acc» can stand for «according (to)», «accompanied» or «accommodation». In text messages, it can mean «actually», as in «I acc love this song». Ask yourself: which full word would fit this sentence best? Then try it and check that it makes sense.
fact: An abbreviation is a short form of a word or phrase.
fact: «Acc.» is short for «account», as in a bank account.
fact: «Acc.» can also be short for «accusative», a grammar case in German, Latin and Ukrainian.
fact: In notes and adverts, «acc» can mean «according (to)», «accompanied» or «accommodation».
fact: In texting, «acc» can mean «actually»; you see it in writing and do not say it aloud.
exercise: The bank letter says «Your acc. balance is £40.» What does acc. mean here? | *Account | Accompanied | Accusative | Actually
exercise: In a German or Latin grammar book you see «acc.» after a noun. What does it stand for? | Account, a bank record | Accommodation | According (to) | *Accusative, a grammar case
exercise: Ella texts, «I acc love this song». What does acc most likely mean? | Accompanied | *Actually | Account | Accommodation
test: In a holiday advert, «Acc. included: breakfast and wifi» tells you the place to stay is included. What does acc. stand for? | Accusative | Actually | *Accommodation | Account
test: Notes say «acc. to the teacher, we finish at three.» What does acc. mean here? | Accompanied | Accusative | Account | *According (to)
exam: Which statement about «acc» is correct? | *It can be short for several different words, depending on where you see it | It only ever means account | It means very old | It is a long word that you must say aloud
